{
  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_017",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 4.1 Low Density Residential Development\n\nClause 4.1 - land_use_zoning (land_use_zoning): LOWDENSITY RESIDENTIAL DEVELOPMENT\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To provide more details on the residential standards contained in Marrickville Local Environmental Plan 2011 (MLEP 2011).\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To maintain and encourage compatible architectural styles within residential areas.\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (environmental_protection): To encourage residential development which is sensitive to the local environment, socially responsive and which promotes a safe living environment and makes better use of existing infrastructure.\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To ensure the impact of urban housing on the amenity of surrounding properties and the streetscape is a prime and initial consideration in the preparation and assessment of development proposals.\n\nClause 4.1.1 - heritage (development_control): To encourage restoration and sympathetic alterations and additions to residential period buildings in a manner that retains and enhances their architectural character and streetscape presentation.\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To require high quality urban design and accessible and adaptable accommodation.\n\nClause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To encourage innovative design that positively responds to the character and context of the locality.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 4.1 Low Density Residential Development",
    "extractions_count": 8
  }
}